[
    {
        "content": "<p>I was working on some <code>Fintype</code> instance diamonds, and I wondered again if it is possible to get rid of the annoyance of <code>Fintype</code> instance diamonds. Because, when doing proofs about finite types, there is no mathematical content in the definitional equality checking of <code>Fintype</code> instances - it is just an annoying thing that you have to watch out for.</p>\n<p>There seem to be two main reasons to use <code>Fintype</code> over <code>Finite</code>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Executable code, i.e. supporting <code>#eval</code></li>\n<li>Definitional reduction, i.e. supporting <code>rfl</code>/<code>decide</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For (2), we can work around this by using some other tactics (maybe <code>cbv</code>, or maybe a new one). But for (1), it is not so obvious how we can work around this. So, I'd like to propose that <code>@[csimp]</code> could be made stronger. In particular, <code>@[csimp]</code> lemmas should be able to synthesize instances such as <code>Fintype</code> or <code>Decidable</code>.</p>\n<p>Could such a feature be in scope for the compiler? Or is there some reason why <code>csimp</code> can only ever work with equalities between constants?</p>\n<p>Note that a concept of rewrite rules in the compiler <a href=\"https://wiki.haskell.org/GHC/Using_rules\">does exist in Haskell</a>, so this may also be a useful feature for people writing code in Lean.</p>",
        "id": 592776688,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777909592
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you show concrete examples of the things you want to be transformed?</p>",
        "id": 592778402,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1777910063
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's an example of what I have in mind:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univ'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">haveI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofFinite</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">univ</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">csimp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univ'_eq_univ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">univ'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">univ'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100000</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 4999950000</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univ'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100000</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It would be nice if we could use the version of <code>univ</code> that takes <code>Finite</code> as an assumption, so that any two <code>univ</code> are definitionally equal. And then the compiler should be able to turn this into the version that takes <code>Fintype</code> as an assumption, so that is is computable.</p>",
        "id": 592786941,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777912386
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right, in general it is of course difficult to have <code>csimp</code> apply lemmas that have arbitrary arguments because the LCNF of an arbitrary lean expression can look quite different from the Lean expression itself. Maybe in this particular case something could be done about it because all the arguments are just parameters from the theorem though I'm unsure if people are going to be satisfied by that.</p>",
        "id": 593226409,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1778065655
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would it be possible to run <code>csimp</code> lemmas as a simp set in the <code>simp</code> tactic? Or does the transformation have to be done in the LCNF representation?</p>",
        "id": 593228881,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1778066496
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, this is something I was wondering/experimenting about for quite some time too. </p>\n<p>I have some experiments in this direction. I have a metaprogram that takes a Lean declaration and runs it through specially configured <code>simp</code> doing all kinds of rewrites like that, defines a new declaration and then adds a new <code>implemented_by</code>.</p>\n<p>I did these experiments some time ago, but if I remember correctly I relativelly quickly ran into performance issue as running <code>simp</code> on every used declaration got slow pretty quickly.</p>",
        "id": 593267378,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778076116
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is behaving sort of like marking everything with <code>@[specialize]</code> and using <code>simp</code> to do the specialization.</p>",
        "id": 593268638,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778076344
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"346070\">@Tomas Skrivan</span>, did you use the standard <code>simp</code> set? I would expect that with a small set of rewrite lemmas this should be reasonably fast.</p>",
        "id": 593302185,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1778084033
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think I did use standard simp set but I think it really depends on what kind of can of worms do you hit if you eagerly specialize every single declaration you encounter :) I will try to dig out the code so you can play with it.</p>",
        "id": 593303634,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778084412
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One thing I also did is to pull/push code along <code>Equiv</code> so I can replace one type for another like <code>Fin n -&gt; A</code> for <code>Vector A n</code> and let simp eliminate all the equivalence maps.</p>",
        "id": 593304016,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778084522
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, we could go a step further where we change the definition of <code>Finset</code> to be a 2 field structure of a <code>Finite</code> <code>Set</code>, so that it has no computational content. And then make the compiler replace it with what we now call <code>Finset</code>. But this sounds a lot harder to implement than what I proposed above.</p>",
        "id": 593304967,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1778084812
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My previous experimentation was part of another project and very messy. I used AI to extract a smaller and cleaner prototype <a href=\"https://github.com/lecopivo/LeanSAS\">https://github.com/lecopivo/LeanSAS</a></p>\n<p>You can write things like </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">boolNotNot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">sas</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">not_not</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">boolNotNot</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which defines <code>boolNotNot._spec</code> which runs  <code>simp only [Bool.not_not]</code> on the definition of <code>boolNotNot</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- info: def LeanSASTests.boolNotNotOnly._spec : Bool → Bool :=</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">fun b =&gt; b -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">print</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">boolNotNotOnly</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">spec</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The command <code>#sas</code> has similar notation as <code>simp</code>.</p>\n<p>A more complicated example trying to match yours example without mathlib. There are two classes <code>SlowEnum A</code> and <code>FastEnum A</code> and theorem</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univSlow_eq_univFast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FastEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">univSlow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univFast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>rewriting <code>univSlow</code> to <code>univFast</code> if possible.</p>\n<p>Here is the code </p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>code</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">elems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FastEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fastElems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fast_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum.elems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fastElems</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univSlow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum.elems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univFast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FastEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">FastEnum.fastElems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univSlow_eq_univFast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FastEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">univSlow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univFast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univSlow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">univFast</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FastEnum.fast_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">elems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Small.a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small.b</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FastEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fastElems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Small.a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small.b</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fast_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smallCode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small.a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">10</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small.b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">20</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">genericSum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SlowEnum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">univSlow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">foldl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smallSum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">genericSum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Small</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smallCode</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">sas</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smallSum</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: def LeanSASTests.smallSum._spec : Nat :=</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">genericSum_sas_1 -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"k\">#print</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smallSum._spec</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: def LeanSASTests.genericSum_sas_1 : Nat :=</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">List.foldl (fun acc x =&gt; acc + smallCode x) 0 univFast -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"k\">#print</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">genericSum_sas_1</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>\n<p>The main thing to notice is that <code>#print genericSum_sas_1</code> has <code>univFast</code> in its definition and not <code>univSlow</code> as <code>genericSum</code>.</p>",
        "id": 593360419,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778101531
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Of course, now you can easily define your own version of <code>#eval e</code> which expands to something like:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">sas_eval_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">sas</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">sas_eval_expr</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">sas_eval_expr</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">spec</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 593360959,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778101717
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One thing to look out is that <code>#sas f</code> currently specializes only definitions in the same root namespace as <code>f</code>. This is to prevent some crazy descends into core Lean and infinite loops like <code>a + b = unfold =&gt; Nat.add a b = simp =&gt; a + b = unfold =&gt; ...</code>.</p>",
        "id": 593361598,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1778101955
    }
]